A||||7||N_Man||which struts are better?||||5||
Z||000000||N_Man||08-16-2000||12:53 PM||||What struts are better gas charged or not gas charged.<P>A friend of mine replaced his rear struts and springs to a gas charged strut and eibach lowering springs but still has the same ride height.<P>Im just going to change the struts and use a set of stock springs but dont want my car to sit any higher.  What should I use?||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||08-16-2000||01:05 PM||||He used gas charged and Eibachs and the car sits higher? <P>I've run Koni's, KYB, and Bilsteins. I prefer the KYB's for a good cost/performance balance. Gas charged.<P>I have them on one of my 86SE's and it's definitely lower than stock. <P>Terry<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000002||Oreif||08-16-2000||01:09 PM||||I have KYB's and Eibach springs and my car is 1.2" lower than stock. If your friend has Eibach's and the ride height didn't change something is amiss. The Eibachs are physically shorter than the stock springs. Is he sure his car wasn't lowered to begin with? Is he sure he bought the correct Eibach springs?||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||08-16-2000||06:55 PM||||I like KYB also. Koni are to stiff/expensive. I have Monroes on now as I didn't have the $ for KYB at the last change. They are ok but I wouldn't call them performance, just cheap. Look at the past posts on suspension mods in the archives. It depends what other mods your going to make, what your goal is, as to handeling. Do you want gokart/hard ride or soft.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-16-2000||09:03 PM||||KYB is now only slightly more than Monroe. You can find none gas charged struts? I didn't think anyone still made them. Gas struts and shocks will always out perform non gased ones.<P>You friend sure he go the right struts? There are struts that will bolt in but have the spring seat at the wrong hieght.||||reg||1
Z||000005||N_Man||08-16-2000||11:23 PM||||His struts are monroe senatrac.<BR>same ride height as before the change the springs do sit loose on the strut.  So it might make sense if they are the wrong strut for his application<P>But you guys think KYB is the best choice for the money.  I dont mind spending a little more but not lots.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||08-17-2000||12:23 AM||||I may have missunderstood you terryk, but if I put KYB shocks and struts on my Fiero it will ride lower?  Im pretty sure the shocks on there now are the original.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Stering wheel<BR>Gas AND brake petals<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||10
Z||000007||theogre||08-17-2000||12:05 PM||||Gas charged struts/shocks WILL NOT hold up a car by themselves. Something is definatly wrong of the springs are loose.<P>Shocks/struts generally will not make any change to ride hieght that you'd notice. The perpose of the gas in them is to kill cavitation so it won't foam the oil thus reducing effectiveness of the shock,strut. ||||reg||1
